Subject: [PATCH] gui_test: use standard evdev key values

The LinHT keypad driver reported every key inverted (0 on press, 1 on release),
and gui_test was written against that. With the driver fixed
(meta-linht-hardware: matrix-keypad report presses as 1), a press is 1 again.
Both changes must ship together: with only one of them, PTT would key the
transmitter on release.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [interim: the LVGL Radio app replaces gui_test, docs/architecture.md D30]
---
--- a/tests/gui_test/test.c
+++ b/tests/gui_test/test.c
@@ -24,9 +24,9 @@
 #include <sqlite3.h>
 #include "settings.h"
 
-// keymap states
-#define KEY_PRESS 0
-#define KEY_RELEASE 1
+// keymap states: standard evdev values (the fixed keypad driver reports 1 on press)
+#define KEY_PRESS 1
+#define KEY_RELEASE 0
 
 #define arrlen(x) (sizeof(x) / sizeof(*x))
 
